 [17592186378725 1113 #uuid "883193fd-f5be-5d1c-8ffa-32b09d1431cb" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378725 1145 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=0$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is upward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨1,0,x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower hemisphere ${S}_{2}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=1,\\,Q=0,\\,R=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-1\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-0\\cdot \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}-x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{align