/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14073335/assets/01779de50ae00cf2883bee0e021638a423989b87a69aaa17e0332c4a671a32ca.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F=⟨-y,\\,z,\\,0⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that represents the boundary of the solid shown above. Let $D$ be the projection of the solid onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378732 1113 #uuid "39e1c3e2-6428-5a2a-8b1d-95017ac2ef6f" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378732 1145 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=0$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is upward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨-y,z,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}0\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower cone ${S}_{2}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4)=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4)=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=-y,\\,Q=z=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4,\\,R=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-(-y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-4)\\cdot \\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y+\\frac{4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y-\\frac{xy+4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & =0+{∬}_{D}y-\\frac{xy+4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}y-\\frac{xy+4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378734 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378735 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378736 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378737 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378738 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1041 "selection" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378735 13194139535996 true] [17592186378733 1110 #uuid "c36c108b-f740-54fa-805a-1ad869b6e112" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378734 1034 "xy-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535996 true] [17592186378734 1111 #uuid "eee982ac-cfca-5d03-a57c-278b2d139100" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378735 1034 "y-\\frac{xy+4y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535996 true] [17592186378735 1111 #uuid "d15df8d0-78cb-5542-9a8e-1d2392044cff" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378736 1034 "y-xy\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" 13194139535996 true] [17592186378736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535996 true] [17592186378736 1111 #uuid "6c8e1246-763b-5440-86da-c1ebeb83a284" 13194139535996 true] [175921